    {
      "key": "team.listening.b2.how-do-we-launch-things-into-space.32ecf094a6244b0ba0c1c6a0ddde0c1d",
      "kind": "ListeningTranscriptLine",
      "values": {
        "OrderIndex": 4,
        "Speaker": "Narrator",
        "Text": "Why rockets? A spacecraft \u2013 and basically everything else on Earth \u2013 is held down by Earth\u2019s gravity.",
        "VietnameseMeaning": "V\u00EC sao l\u1EA1i l\u00E0 t\u00EAn l\u1EEDa? M\u1ED9t t\u00E0u v\u0169 tr\u1EE5 \u2013 v\u00E0 v\u1EC1 c\u01A1 b\u1EA3n m\u1ECDi th\u1EE9 kh\u00E1c tr\u00EAn Tr\u00E1i \u0110\u1EA5t \u2013 b\u1ECB gi\u1EEF l\u1EA1i b\u1EDFi l\u1EF1c h\u1EA5p d\u1EABn c\u1EE7a Tr\u00E1i \u0110\u1EA5t.",
        "StartTime": 25.6,
        "EndTime": 33.7
      },
      "references": {
        "LessonId": "team.listening.b2.how-do-we-launch-things-into-space"
      }
    },
    {
