      "kind": "ListeningQuizQuestion",
      "values": {
        "OrderIndex": 4,
        "QuestionText": "Why does a satellite stay in orbit?",
        "OptionA": "A balance between its momentum and Earth\u0027s gravity",
        "OptionB": "It has an engine that never stops",
        "OptionC": "The Moon pulls it",
        "OptionD": "The wind pushes it",
        "CorrectAnswer": "A",
        "Explanation": "\u0022This happens because there is a balance between the energy the satellite picked up from the rocket \u2013 called momentum \u2013\u0022 \u2014 01:21"
